  "goodToKnow": "Der Herzinfarkt is a heart attack: einen Herzinfarkt erleiden. If you suspect one in Germany, call 112, the European emergency number. Typical signs are chest pain spreading to the arm, shortness of breath and nausea, and in women often less typical symptoms. A stroke is der Schlaganfall, and cardiac arrest der Herzstillstand. Casually, Germans joke Ich krieg gleich einen Herzinfarkt! (I'm going to have a heart attack!). Plural: die Herzinfarkte."
